hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1682","Narrated to us Abu Zuhayr ‘Abd al-Majid ibn Ibrahim al-Misri, narrated to us ‘Amr ibn Hashim—meaning al-Bayruniyy—who said: al-Awza‘i narrated to me, Musa ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said:\nA woman passed by Abu Hurayrah (RA) and the fragrance of her perfume was wafting strongly. He said to her, “Where are you going, O slave of al-Jabbar?”\nShe said, “To the mosque.”\nHe said, “Did you apply perfume?”\nShe said, “Yes.”\nHe said, “Then go back and perform ghusl (ritual bath), for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say:\n‘Allah does not accept the prayer of a woman who comes out to the mosque with strong perfume until she returns and performs ghusl.’”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
